# Manual Content Mode

When CTO provides full file content, Cursor must follow strict write behavior.

## Required write behavior

- Write to the exact file path provided
- Overwrite the file with supplied content
- Preserve original newlines and line breaks
- Do not paraphrase or summarize supplied content
- Do not collapse multiple lines into one line
- Do not optimize or refactor unless explicitly requested

## Forbidden behavior

- Do not merge partial edits when full file content was supplied
- Do not convert Python, Markdown, or MDC into single-line format
- Do not drop blank lines that appear in supplied content

## After writing

- Run required format checks when specified by task
- Run python -m pytest when Python files changed
- Report written paths and test outcomes
